---
import { Font } from 'astro:assets';
import Bare from '../../layouts/Bare.astro';

const wikis = [
  ['all', 'Every Wikipedia'],
  ['en', 'English'],
  ['de', 'German'],
  ['fr', 'French'],
  ['es', 'Spanish'],
  ['it', 'Italian'],
  ['pt', 'Portuguese'],
  ['nl', 'Dutch'],
  ['pl', 'Polish'],
  ['sv', 'Swedish'],
  ['ru', 'Russian'],
  ['uk', 'Ukrainian'],
  ['ja', 'Japanese'],
  ['zh', 'Chinese'],
];
---

<Bare
  title="Arrivals"
  description="A split-flap arrivals board for Wikipedia: every row is an edit landing somewhere in the world right now."
>
  <Font cssVariable="--font-flap" slot="head" />

  <main class="hall" data-arrivals>
    <a class="home" href="/">thesandbox.page</a>

    <div class="dock" data-dock>
      <section class="board" data-board aria-label="Arrivals board">
        <header class="board-head">
          <div class="board-title">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true">
              <path
                d="M3 27h26v2H3zM4.2 16.4l2.3-.6 3 2.6 5.2-1.4-4.6-8.4 2.8-.8 8 7 5.6-1.5a2 2 0 0 1 1 3.9L8.6 22.3z"
                fill="currentColor"></path>
            </svg>
            <h1>Arrivals</h1>
          </div>
          <p class="board-sub">Wikipedia edits, as they land</p>
          <div class="clock" data-clock role="img"></div>
        </header>

        <div class="grid" data-grid></div>

        <footer class="board-foot" data-foot data-state="connecting">
          <span class="status"><span class="status-lamp"></span><span data-status>Connecting</span></span>
          <span class="tally" data-tally aria-live="off"></span>
          <span class="holding" data-hold hidden>Holding while you look</span>
        </footer>
      </section>

      <div class="away" data-away hidden>
        <p>The board is in its own window, floating over everything else.</p>
        <button type="button" data-return>Bring it back</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="controls">
      <label class="from">
        <span>From</span>
        <select data-wiki>{wikis.map(([value, name]) => <option value={value}>{name}</option>)}</select>
      </label>
      <button type="button" data-bots aria-pressed="false">Hide bots</button>
      <button type="button" data-sound aria-pressed="false">Sound off</button>
      <button type="button" data-pop aria-pressed="false" hidden>Pop out</button>
    </div>
    <p class="pop-note" data-pop-note hidden>
      Chrome, Edge, and Firefox 151 or later can pop the board out into a window that stays on top of everything.
    </p>
  </main>

  <article class="notes">
    <h2>What's landing</h2>
    <p>
      Every row is an edit to a Wikipedia article, seconds old. <strong>From</strong> is the language
      edition, <strong>Bytes</strong> is how much the article grew or shrank, and <strong>Remarks</strong> says what
      kind of edit it was: a new page, a revert, a bot, an editor without an account, or a minor fix. Ordinary edits have simply
      landed. Click a row to open the change on Wikipedia.
    </p>
    <p>
      Wikipedia takes far more edits than a board can show, so this is a sample. Once the board has settled, it waits a
      few seconds, then brings in the newest arrival and pushes the rest down a row, the way a real board does. Point at
      the board and it holds still until you let go.
    </p>

    <h2>How the flaps work</h2>
    <p>
      Each character is a drum of printed flaps, in a fixed order: a blank, the alphabet, the digits, then punctuation.
      To change from <code>D</code> to <code>B</code>, a cell can't skip ahead; it flips through every flap
      from <code>E</code> round to <code>B</code>. That's why some cells settle at once and others clatter on for
      seconds, and why the whole board ripples instead of updating in one go.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every flip is two half-flaps. The top half falls from upright to flat, still showing the old character, and the
      bottom half carries on from flat to hanging, showing the new one, with a small bounce at the stop. There is no
      canvas and no animation library: each cell is four <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> halves,
      turned with <code>rotateX()</code> in one shared <code>requestAnimationFrame</code> loop. Accents, Cyrillic, and
      kanji aren't printed on the drum, so their cells rattle through a few random flaps and then show the character anyway.
      Right-to-left and shaped scripts, such as Arabic and Hindi, come apart one character to a cell, so the board
      skips their titles. The sound is made on the spot with Web Audio: a burst of noise a few milliseconds long,
      filtered to a hard plastic tick, layered more thickly as more flaps land at once.
    </p>

    <h2>Popping out</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Pop out</strong> uses the Document Picture-in-Picture API to move the live board, not a copy, into a
      small window that stays on top of your other apps. The page copies its styles across, hands the board's animation
      loop and timers to the new window so it keeps moving after you switch tabs, and takes the board back when you
      close the window.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the edits come from</h2>
    <p>
      Wikimedia publishes every change to its wikis as a public stream of server-sent events, which the page reads with
      an <code>EventSource</code>. If the stream goes quiet, the page polls each wiki's recent-changes API instead, and
      the footer says so. Reverts are a guess from the edit summary, which is free text, so some slip through.
    </p>
    <p class="credits">
      Edit data from <a href="https://wikitech.wikimedia.org/wiki/Event_Platform/EventStreams_HTTP_Service"
        >Wikimedia EventStreams</a
      > and the MediaWiki API. Set in <a href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Roboto+Condensed">Roboto Condensed</a>,
      SIL Open Font License, served from this site.
    </p>
  </article>
</Bare>

<script>
  import { startArrivals } from './_app';

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-arrivals]');
  if (root) startArrivals(root);
</script>

<style is:global>
  /* Global on purpose: the board's rows and cells are built by script, and the
     same rules have to follow the board into a picture-in-picture window. */

  :root {
    --hall: #0b0c0e;
    --housing: #141518;
    --housing-edge: #26282d;
    --flap-top: #2a2b2f;
    --flap-top-end: #232428;
    --flap-bottom: #1e1f22;
    --flap-bottom-end: #19191c;
    --ink: #f3f0e6;
    --sign: #ffc634;
    --muted: #8d8a82;
    --kind-new: #5fd68a;
    --kind-revert: #ff6a55;
    --kind-bot: #7fb2ff;
    --kind-anon: #e8b04a;
    --flap-font: var(--font-flap), 'Arial Narrow', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 70% at 50% -10%, #23201a 0%, transparent 60%),
      var(--hall);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 400 1rem/1.6 var(--flap-font);
  }

  .hall {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    min-height: 100dvh;
    padding: 4.5rem 1rem 3rem;
    display: grid;
    align-content: center;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .home {
    position: absolute;
    top: 1.25rem;
    left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .home:hover,
  .home:focus-visible {
    color: var(--sign);
  }

  .dock {
    width: min(100%, 72rem);
  }

  /* The board. */

  .board {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    padding: clamp(0.75rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--housing-edge);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    background: linear-gradient(#18191c, var(--housing));
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 1px 0 #ffffff12,
      inset 0 -2px 0 #00000080,
      0 2rem 4rem -1rem #000000d0;
  }

  .board-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    column-gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(0.6rem, 1.6vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--sign);
  }

  .board-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6em;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4.4vw, 2.6rem);
  }

  .board-title svg {
    width: 1.1em;
    height: 1.1em;
    flex: none;
  }

  .board-title h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font: 700 1em/1 var(--flap-font);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .board-sub {
    grid-row: 2;
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 1.6vw, 0.9rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .clock {
    grid-row: 1 / 3;
    grid-column: 2;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.12em;
    --u: clamp(1.1rem, 3.4vw, 2rem);
  }

  .clock .cell {
    font-size: calc(var(--u) * 1.12);
  }

  .colon {
    font: 700 calc(var(--u) * 1.1) / 1 var(--flap-font);
    color: var(--ink);
    animation: blink 2s steps(1) infinite;
  }

  @keyframes blink {
    50% {
      opacity: 0.2;
    }
  }

  .grid {
    container-type: inline-size;
    display: grid;
    gap: calc(100cqi / var(--units) * 0.32);
  }

  .grid > .row {
    --u: calc(100cqi / var(--units));
  }

  .row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: calc(var(--u) * 0.8);
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: calc(var(--u) * 0.15);
    outline-offset: calc(var(--u) * 0.2);
  }

  .row[href]:hover .cell,
  .row[href]:focus-visible .cell {
    --flap-top: #34353a;
    --flap-top-end: #2c2d31;
    --flap-bottom: #26272b;
    --flap-bottom-end: #202124;
  }

  .row.head {
    color: var(--sign);
    font: 700 calc(var(--u) * 0.62) / 1 var(--flap-font);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .row.head .col {
    width: calc(var(--u) * (var(--w) - 0.12));
  }

  .row.head .col-change {
    text-align: right;
  }

  .lamp {
    flex: none;
    width: calc(var(--u) * 0.5);
    height: calc(var(--u) * 0.5);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #2b2c30;
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 1px #00000080;
    transition:
      background-color 0.4s,
      box-shadow 0.4s;
  }

  .row.head .lamp {
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .row[data-kind='new'] .lamp {
    --lit: var(--kind-new);
  }
  .row[data-kind='revert'] .lamp {
    --lit: var(--kind-revert);
  }
  .row[data-kind='bot'] .lamp {
    --lit: var(--kind-bot);
  }
  .row[data-kind='anon'] .lamp {
    --lit: var(--kind-anon);
  }

  .row[data-kind] .lamp {
    background: var(--lit, #3a3b40);
    box-shadow: 0 0 calc(var(--u) * 0.6) var(--lit, transparent);
  }

  .row[data-kind='new'] .col-remarks {
    color: var(--kind-new);
  }
  .row[data-kind='revert'] .col-remarks {
    color: var(--kind-revert);
  }
  .row[data-kind='bot'] .col-remarks {
    color: var(--kind-bot);
  }
  .row[data-kind='anon'] .col-remarks {
    color: var(--kind-anon);
  }

  .col {
    display: flex;
    flex: none;
    gap: calc(var(--u) * 0.12);
  }

  /* One character: a still top and bottom, and two flaps that move. */

  .cell {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    flex: none;
    width: calc(var(--u) * 0.88);
    height: calc(var(--u) * 1.45);
    perspective: calc(var(--u) * 5);
    font: 700 calc(var(--u) * 1.12) / 1 var(--flap-font);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .clock .cell {
    width: calc(var(--u) * 0.88);
    height: calc(var(--u) * 1.45);
  }

  .half {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 50%;
    overflow: hidden;
    backface-visibility: hidden;
  }

  .half > span {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 200%;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }

  .half > .wide {
    font-size: 0.74em;
  }

  .half.top {
    top: 0;
    border-radius: calc(var(--u) * 0.1) calc(var(--u) * 0.1) 0 0;
    background: linear-gradient(var(--flap-top), var(--flap-top-end));
    transform-origin: 50% 100%;
  }

  .half.top > span {
    top: 0;
  }

  .half.bottom {
    bottom: 0;
    border-radius: 0 0 calc(var(--u) * 0.1) calc(var(--u) * 0.1);
    background: linear-gradient(var(--flap-bottom), var(--flap-bottom-end));
    transform-origin: 50% 0;
  }

  .half.bottom > span {
    bottom: 0;
  }

  .flap {
    display: none;
    z-index: 1;
    will-change: transform;
  }

  .flipping .flap {
    display: block;
  }

  /* The hinge: a hairline gap where the two halves meet. */
  .cell::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 2;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: calc(50% - 0.5px);
    height: 1px;
    background: #000000b0;
  }

  .board-foot {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.4rem;
    margin-top: clamp(0.6rem, 1.6vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 1.5vw, 0.85rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .status {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5em;
  }

  .status-lamp {
    width: 0.6em;
    height: 0.6em;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--muted);
  }

  [data-state='live'] .status-lamp {
    background: var(--kind-new);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0.6em var(--kind-new);
    animation: blink 2.4s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  [data-state='polling'] .status-lamp {
    background: var(--kind-anon);
  }

  [data-state='down'] .status-lamp {
    background: var(--kind-revert);
  }

  .holding {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--sign);
  }

  .holding[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .away {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 3rem 1rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--housing-edge);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .away[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .away p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Controls. */

  .controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .controls button,
  .away button,
  .from {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    min-height: 2.5rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--housing-edge);
    border-radius: 0.35rem;
    background: var(--housing);
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 700 0.85rem/1 var(--flap-font);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .controls button:hover,
  .away button:hover,
  .from:hover {
    border-color: var(--muted);
  }

  .controls button[aria-pressed='true'] {
    border-color: var(--sign);
    color: var(--sign);
  }

  .controls button[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .from {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .from span {
    color: var(--sign);
  }

  .from select {
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    font: inherit;
    letter-spacing: inherit;
    text-transform: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .from select option {
    background: var(--housing);
  }

  .pop-note {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .pop-note[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Notes under the board. */

  .notes {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1rem 5rem;
    color: #c9c5bb;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .notes h2 {
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0.6rem;
    color: var(--sign);
    font: 700 1rem/1.2 var(--flap-font);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .notes strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .notes code {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }

  .notes a {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .credits {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* Popped out: the board fills its own small window. */

  body.pip {
    display: grid;
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--housing);
  }

  body.pip .board {
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    box-shadow: none;
    padding: 4vw;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .colon,
    [data-state='live'] .status-lamp {
      animation: none;
    }
  }
</style>
